A||||5||lowfunds||Broken rear cradle bolts||||8||
Z||000000||lowfunds||04-23-2001||11:49 AM||||%$#^#$ stupid cradle bolts. Its times like this I wish I lived in a winter free state. Has anyone had the top nut break loose? If so what is the best way to reweld it? Both nuts on the rear of my car broke loose, So I had to cut the heads off. Question is what is the best way to fix? Do I remove the plate on the bottom and replace it with a new assembly? Or can I just tack the nut from the bottom? Also can you still get the cradle bolts and washers oem? thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||skitime||04-23-2001||12:07 PM||||I had to cut the bolts off of one in a junkyard just like you did.  Of course I didn't have to repair it but it made me think about what I would do if it happened to my car.  I think I would cut a steel plate the width of the inside of the frame rail and weld a nut to it in the correct location. Another possibility would be to cut an access hole on the wheel side of the frame and insert a large washer and nut but cutting the frame rail might slightly weaken the area.  Just my thoughts, hope it helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jimmy||04-23-2001||12:25 PM||||I had the same problem.  Had to cut three slots into the side of the frame, above the bolt, to form make a tab.  Bent that tab down and was able to keep the pseudo nut from spinning.  You can weld it all back up when your done if you want.  A cutting wheel makes quick work of the frame.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||04-23-2001||02:28 PM||||Same thing happen when I got my clutch done.  They cut a small square out of the frame with a torch (cutting wheel is fine) then welded in a new nut.  Yup, sounds like you need to do some cutting...||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||04-23-2001||03:08 PM||||Yup, I cut a hole in the side of my frame to grab that nut with a vicegrip.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowfunds||04-23-2001||04:24 PM||||Thanks guys. About the craddle bolts? Are they still availiable? Or can someone tell me what size they are. I can't measure mine very accuratly because of torching the heads off. Thanks again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
